IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa24-delivery.l4: Part 35 "Supplementary provisions", ss 1111 and 1113 to 1120 of the Companies Act 2006 (lines 15970-15977
-- and 16011-16057 of ukpga-2006-46.txt; ss 1112 to 1112B, which sit between them, are in coa24-false-statements.l4).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE ANSWERS FOR THE OTHER PARTS. The Act's index (Schedule 8) says "document" in Part 35 is defined by
-- s 1114(1): `s 1114(1)(a) the thing is a document in Part 35`; and "registrar's rules" by s 1117.
--
-- WHAT IS NOT ENCODED. ss 1116(2)-(4) and 1117(1)-(2) are regulation-making and rule-making powers: machinery, inert
-- (reason 2) in NOTES.md. ss 1115(1) and 1120 are shown repealed or omitted in the text.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29; assumed, not ruled by a lawyer). MAYBE answers: JUST TRUE is the text
-- saying yes; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words (each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"`); NOTHING is "not covered" (each NOTHING branch says why,
-- as `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`). A function whose name ends "meets the requirement of s N" answers JUST FALSE when the
-- "must" it cites is not done: that is a fork line in NOTES.md, not a ruling.

§ `Part 35: supplementary provisions (ss 1111 and 1113 to 1120)`

-- ---- s 1111 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15972 | (1) Where a document required or authorised to be delivered to the registrar under any enactment is required—
-- src:15973 | (a) to be certified as an accurate translation or transliteration, or
-- src:15974 | (b) to be certified as a correct copy or verified,
-- src:15975 | the registrar may impose requirements as to the person, or description of person, by whom the certificate or verification is to be given.
@ref s 1111(1) The registrar may impose requirements as to who gives a certificate or verification (src:15972-15975)
GIVEN `the document is required or authorised to be delivered to the registrar under an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is required to be certified as an accurate translation or transliteration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is required to be certified as a correct copy or verified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1111(1) the registrar may impose requirements as to the person by whom the certificate or verification is to be given` MEANS
    IF `the document is required or authorised to be delivered to the registrar under an enactment` AND (`the document is required to be certified as an accurate translation or transliteration` OR `the document is required to be certified as a correct copy or verified`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a document required or authorised to be delivered to the registrar under any enactment is required— (a) to be certified as an accurate translation or transliteration, or (b) to be certified as a correct copy or verified"

-- src:15976 | (2) The power conferred by section 1068 (registrar's requirements as to form, authentication and manner of delivery) is exercisable in relation to the certificate or verification as if it were a separate document.
@ref s 1111(2) Section 1068 applies to the certificate or verification as if it were a separate document (src:15976)
GIVEN `the certificate or verification is one to which a requirement under subsection (1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1111(2) the power conferred by section 1068 is exercisable in relation to the certificate or verification as if it were a separate document` MEANS
    IF `the certificate or verification is one to which a requirement under subsection (1) applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to the certificate or verification" under this section

-- src:15977 | (3) Requirements imposed under this section must not be inconsistent with requirements imposed by any enactment with respect to the certification or verification of the document concerned.
@ref s 1111(3) The requirements must not be inconsistent with requirements imposed by any enactment (src:15977)
GIVEN `the requirement is inconsistent with a requirement imposed by an enactment with respect to the certification or verification of the document concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1111(3) the registrar may impose the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the requirement is inconsistent with a requirement imposed by an enactment with respect to the certification or verification of the document concerned`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Requirements imposed under this section must not be inconsistent with requirements imposed by any enactment with respect to the certification or verification of the document concerned"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection bars inconsistent requirements; it does not itself grant the power, which is in subsection (1)

-- ---- s 1113 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1113 person who may act` IS ONE OF
    `s 1113 the registrar`
    `s 1113 a member of the company`
    `s 1113 a creditor of the company`
    `s 1113 some other person`

-- src:16012 | (1) This section applies where a company has made default in complying with any obligation under the Companies Acts—
-- src:16013 | (a) to deliver a document to the registrar, or
-- src:16014 | (b) to give notice to the registrar of any matter.
@ref s 1113(1) The section applies where a company has made default in delivering a document or giving notice (src:16012-16014)
GIVEN `the company has made default in complying with an obligation under the Companies Acts to deliver a document to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has made default in complying with an obligation under the Companies Acts to give notice to the registrar of any matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1113(1) the section applies` MEANS
    IF `the company has made default in complying with an obligation under the Companies Acts to deliver a document to the registrar` OR `the company has made default in complying with an obligation under the Companies Acts to give notice to the registrar of any matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where a company has made default in complying with any obligation under the Companies Acts— (a) to deliver a document to the registrar, or (b) to give notice to the registrar of any matter"

-- src:16015 | (2) The registrar, or any member or creditor of the company, may give notice to the company requiring it to comply with the obligation.
@ref s 1113(2) The registrar, or any member or creditor, may give notice requiring the company to comply (src:16015)
GIVEN `the section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 1113 person who may act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1113(2) the person may give notice to the company requiring it to comply with the obligation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the section applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER person
        WHEN `s 1113 the registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 1113 a member of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 1113 a creditor of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 1113 some other person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The registrar, or any member or creditor of the company, may give notice" names who may and does not say that no one else may
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only where section 1113 applies

-- (3): "within 14 days after service of the notice": the day of service is not counted, so the last day is 14 days after it.
-- src:16016 | (3) If the company fails to make good the default within 14 days after service of the notice, the registrar, or any member or creditor of the company, may apply to the court for an order directing the company, and any specified officer of it, to make good the default within a specified time.
@ref s 1113(3) The last day for the company to make good the default (src:16016)
GIVEN `date on which the notice was served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1113(3) the last day for the company to make good the default` MEANS `date on which the notice was served` PLUS 14

@ref s 1113(3) The registrar, or any member or creditor, may apply to the court if the company fails to make good the default (src:16016)
GIVEN `the section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 1113 person who may act`
      `date on which the notice was served` IS A DATE
      `date on which the company made good the default` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1113(3) the person may apply to the court for an order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the section applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER person
        WHEN `s 1113 some other person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the registrar, or any member or creditor of the company, may apply to the court"
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `date on which the company made good the default`
            WHEN JUST madeGood THEN
                IF madeGood AT MOST `s 1113(3) the last day for the company to make good the default` `date on which the notice was served`
                THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the company fails to make good the default within 14 days after service of the notice" (it made the default good within the 14 days)
                ELSE JUST TRUE
            WHEN NOTHING THEN
                IF `date on which the question is asked` AT MOST `s 1113(3) the last day for the company to make good the default` `date on which the notice was served`
                THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the company fails to make good the default within 14 days after service of the notice" (the 14 days have not yet ended)
                ELSE JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only where section 1113 applies

-- The company's duty as a regulative rule. The trace clock counts days from the day of service (day 0), and a default made
-- good by day 14 is within "14 days after service".
DECLARE `s 1113(3) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 1113(3) the company`
    `s 1113(3) the person who gave the notice`

DECLARE `s 1113(3) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 1113(3) make good the default`

@ref s 1113(3) The company must make good the default within 14 days after service of the notice (src:16016)
`s 1113(3) the company's duty to make good the default` MEANS
    PARTY `s 1113(3) the company`
    MUST `s 1113(3) make good the default`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 1113(3) the company` BECAUSE "the default was not made good within 14 days after service of the notice"

-- src:16017 | (4) The court's order may provide that all costs (in Scotland, expenses) of or incidental to the application are to be borne by the company or by any officers of it responsible for the default.
@ref s 1113(4) The court's order may provide that costs (in Scotland, expenses) are borne by the company or the officers responsible (src:16017)
GIVEN `the court makes an order on the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1113(4) the court's order may provide that costs are borne by the company or by officers of it responsible for the default` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an order on the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court’s order may provide"

-- src:16018 | (5) This section does not affect the operation of any enactment making it an offence, or imposing a civil penalty, for the default.
@ref s 1113(5) Section 1113 does not affect an enactment making the default an offence or imposing a civil penalty (src:16018)
GIVEN `the enactment makes the default an offence or imposes a civil penalty for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1113(5) section 1113 affects the operation of the enactment` MEANS
    IF `the enactment makes the default an offence or imposes a civil penalty for it`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not affect the operation of any enactment making it an offence, or imposing a civil penalty, for the default"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of an enactment making the default an offence or imposing a civil penalty

-- ---- s 1114 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16020 | (1) In this Part—
-- src:16021 | (a) “document” means information recorded in any form, and
-- src:16022 | (b) references to delivering a document include forwarding, lodging, registering, sending, producing or submitting it or (in the case of a notice) giving it (but do not include the provision of any information by virtue of section 1110E or any other enactment authorising the disclosure of information to the registrar).
@ref s 1114(1)(a) "document" (src:16020-16022)
GIVEN `the thing is information recorded in any form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1114(1)(a) the thing is a document in Part 35` MEANS
    IF `the thing is information recorded in any form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“document” means information recorded in any form"

DECLARE `s 1114(1)(b) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 1114(1)(b) forwarding`
    `s 1114(1)(b) lodging`
    `s 1114(1)(b) registering`
    `s 1114(1)(b) sending`
    `s 1114(1)(b) producing`
    `s 1114(1)(b) submitting`
    `s 1114(1)(b) giving a notice`
    `s 1114(1)(b) providing information by virtue of section 1110E or any other enactment authorising the disclosure of information to the registrar`
    `s 1114(1)(b) some other act`

@ref s 1114(1)(b) References to delivering a document (src:16022)
GIVEN act IS A `s 1114(1)(b) act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1114(1)(b) the act is delivering a document` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 1114(1)(b) forwarding` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1114(1)(b) lodging` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1114(1)(b) registering` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1114(1)(b) sending` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1114(1)(b) producing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1114(1)(b) submitting` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1114(1)(b) giving a notice` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1114(1)(b) providing information by virtue of section 1110E or any other enactment authorising the disclosure of information to the registrar` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(but do not include the provision of any information by virtue of section 1110E or any other enactment authorising the disclosure of information to the registrar)"
    WHEN `s 1114(1)(b) some other act` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to delivering a document include forwarding, lodging, registering, sending, producing or submitting it or (in the case of a notice) giving it"

-- src:16023 | (2) Except as otherwise provided, this Part applies in relation to the supply to the registrar of information otherwise than in documentary form as it applies in relation to the delivery of a document.
@ref s 1114(2) This Part applies to the supply of information otherwise than in documentary form (src:16023)
GIVEN `the information is supplied to the registrar otherwise than in documentary form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `otherwise provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1114(2) Part 35 applies to the supply of the information as it applies to the delivery of a document` MEANS
    IF `the information is supplied to the registrar otherwise than in documentary form` AND (NOT `otherwise provided`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Except as otherwise provided, this Part applies in relation to the supply to the registrar of information otherwise than in documentary form"

-- ---- s 1115 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16026 | (2) A document that is required to be signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar's seal shall, if sent by electronic means, be authenticated in such manner as may be specified by registrar's rules.
@ref s 1115(2) A document to be signed or sealed by the registrar, sent electronically, is authenticated as the registrar's rules specify (src:16026)
GIVEN `the document is required to be signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar's seal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is sent by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1115(2) the document must be authenticated in the manner specified by registrar's rules` MEANS
    IF `the document is required to be signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar's seal` AND `the document is sent by electronic means`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A document that is required to be signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar’s seal shall, if sent by electronic means, be authenticated in such manner as may be specified by registrar’s rules"

-- ---- s 1116 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16028 | (1) Notices that would otherwise need to be published by the registrar in the Gazette may instead be published by such means as may from time to time be approved by the registrar in accordance with regulations made by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 1116(1) Notices may instead be published by approved means (src:16028)
GIVEN `the notice would otherwise need to be published by the registrar in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the means have been approved by the registrar in accordance with regulations made by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1116(1) the notice may instead be published by the approved means` MEANS
    IF `the notice would otherwise need to be published by the registrar in the Gazette` AND `the means have been approved by the registrar in accordance with regulations made by the Secretary of State`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Notices that would otherwise need to be published by the registrar in the Gazette may instead be published by such means as may from time to time be approved by the registrar in accordance with regulations"

-- src:16037 | (5) Before starting to publish notices by means approved under this section the registrar must publish at least one notice to that effect in the Gazette.
@ref s 1116(5) Before using approved means the registrar must publish a notice in the Gazette (src:16037)
GIVEN `the registrar is about to start publishing notices by means approved under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at least one notice to that effect has been published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1116(5) the registrar meets the requirement of s 1116(5)` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the registrar is about to start publishing notices by means approved under this section`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Before starting to publish notices by means approved under this section"
    ELSE IF `at least one notice to that effect has been published in the Gazette`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before starting to publish notices by means approved under this section the registrar must publish at least one notice to that effect in the Gazette"

-- src:16038 | (6) Nothing in this section prevents the registrar from giving public notice both in the Gazette and by means approved under this section.
-- src:16039 | In that case, the requirement of public notice is met when notice is first given by either means.
@ref s 1116(6) The registrar may give public notice both in the Gazette and by approved means; the requirement is met when notice is first given by either (src:16038-16039)
GIVEN `the registrar gives public notice both in the Gazette and by means approved under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1116(6) this section prevents the registrar from giving public notice both in the Gazette and by approved means` MEANS
    IF `the registrar gives public notice both in the Gazette and by means approved under this section`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section prevents the registrar from giving public notice both in the Gazette and by means approved under this section"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of giving public notice both ways

@ref s 1116(6) The day the requirement of public notice is met (src:16039)
GIVEN `date on which notice was first given in the Gazette` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date on which notice was first given by approved means` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 1116(6) the day on which the requirement of public notice is met` MEANS
    CONSIDER `date on which notice was first given in the Gazette`
    WHEN JUST g THEN
        CONSIDER `date on which notice was first given by approved means`
        WHEN JUST m THEN IF g AT MOST m THEN JUST g ELSE JUST m
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST g
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `date on which notice was first given by approved means`

-- ---- s 1117 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16046 | (3) The registrar must—
-- src:16047 | (a) publicise the rules in a manner appropriate to bring them to the notice of persons affected by them, and
-- src:16048 | (b) make copies of the rules available to the public (in hard copy or electronic form).
@ref s 1117(3) The registrar must publicise the rules and make copies available to the public (src:16046-16048)
GIVEN `the rules have been publicised in a manner appropriate to bring them to the notice of persons affected by them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1117(3)(a) the registrar meets the requirement to publicise the rules` MEANS
    IF `the rules have been publicised in a manner appropriate to bring them to the notice of persons affected by them`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar must— (a) publicise the rules in a manner appropriate to bring them to the notice of persons affected by them"

@ref s 1117(3)(b) The registrar must make copies of the rules available to the public in hard copy or electronic form (src:16048)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1117(3)(b) the registrar must make copies of the rules available to the public in the form` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `hard copy form` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `electronic form` THEN JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 1118 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16050 | Nothing in the Companies Acts or any other enactment as to the payment of receipts into the Consolidated Fund shall be read as affecting the operation in relation to the registrar of section 3(1) of the Government Trading Funds Act 1973 (c. 63).
@ref s 1118 Payments into the Consolidated Fund (src:16050)
GIVEN `the provision is one as to the payment of receipts into the Consolidated Fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1118 the provision affects the operation in relation to the registrar of section 3(1) of the Government Trading Funds Act 1973` MEANS
    IF `the provision is one as to the payment of receipts into the Consolidated Fund`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in the Companies Acts or any other enactment as to the payment of receipts into the Consolidated Fund shall be read as affecting the operation in relation to the registrar of section 3(1) of the Government Trading Funds Act 1973"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section speaks only of an enactment as to the payment of receipts into the Consolidated Fund

-- ---- s 1119 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16052 | (1) Where by virtue of an order made under section 69 of the Deregulation and Contracting Out Act 1994 (c. 40) a person is authorised by the registrar to accept delivery of any class of documents that are under any enactment to be delivered to the registrar, the registrar may direct that documents of that class shall be delivered to a specified address of the authorised person.
-- src:16053 | Any such direction must be printed and made available to the public (with or without payment).
@ref s 1119(1) The registrar may direct that documents of the class be delivered to a specified address (src:16052-16053)
GIVEN `by virtue of an order under section 69 of the Deregulation and Contracting Out Act 1994 a person is authorised by the registrar to accept delivery of the class of documents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1119(1) the registrar may direct that documents of the class be delivered to a specified address of the authorised person` MEANS
    IF `by virtue of an order under section 69 of the Deregulation and Contracting Out Act 1994 a person is authorised by the registrar to accept delivery of the class of documents`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where by virtue of an order made under section 69 of the Deregulation and Contracting Out Act 1994 ... a person is authorised by the registrar to accept delivery of any class of documents"

@ref s 1119(1) The direction must be printed and made available to the public (src:16053)
GIVEN `the direction has been printed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction has been made available to the public (with or without payment)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1119(1) the direction meets the requirement of s 1119(1)` MEANS
    IF `the direction has been printed` AND `the direction has been made available to the public (with or without payment)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any such direction must be printed and made available to the public (with or without payment)"

-- src:16054 | (2) A document of that class that is delivered to an address other than the specified address is treated as not having been delivered.
@ref s 1119(2) A document delivered to another address is treated as not having been delivered (src:16054)
GIVEN `a direction has been given for the class of documents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document was delivered to an address other than the specified address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1119(2) the document is treated as delivered` MEANS
    IF `a direction has been given for the class of documents` AND `the document was delivered to an address other than the specified address`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A document of that class that is delivered to an address other than the specified address is treated as not having been delivered"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a document of that class delivered to an address other than the specified address

-- src:16055 | (3) Registrar's rules are not subordinate legislation for the purposes of section 71 of the Deregulation and Contracting Out Act 1994 (functions excluded from contracting out).
@ref s 1119(3) Registrar's rules are not subordinate legislation for the purposes of section 71 of the 1994 Act (src:16055)
GIVEN `the provision is registrar's rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1119(3) the provision is subordinate legislation for the purposes of section 71 of the Deregulation and Contracting Out Act 1994` MEANS
    IF `the provision is registrar's rules`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Registrar’s rules are not subordinate legislation for the purposes of section 71 of the Deregulation and Contracting Out Act 1994"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of registrar's rules
